ormat":"Thumbnail","original":"Snake milking.mkv","mtime":"1663921924","size":"35832","md5":"a3564ffc7be8fd31620d13211d9773df","crc32":"c17a1a20","sha1":"2b10bde2adc66f7a92f1af43dfd3ecc5ad90918e"},{"name":"snake-milking_archive.torrent","source":"metadata","btih":"068ad4d934da215fea3e814372e97ae1d01e8800","mtime":"1663923487","size":"31655","md5":"0b6a35c9695a1c3bb36b91d3dd979354","crc32":"f05b208c","sha1":"c3f28cdc3d34aebf3b57b34c309719fdc058d14c","format":"Archive BitTorrent"},{"name":"snake-milking_files.xml","source":"original","format":"Metadata","md5":"db00420bbf40caca1895855c0a001689","summation":"md5"},{"name":"snake-milking_meta.sqlite","source":"original","mtime":"1663921328","size":"32768","md5":"400e48e665ce087edb0558dd13090f9f","crc32":"b6588fd8","sha1":"33a946f50905050384d16fadc76a6241bd3cc435","format":"Metadata"},{"name":"snake-milking_meta.xml","source":"original","mtime":"1663911899","size":"4225","md5":"32d47a008f5ac3b8c441af226a42ab47","crc32":"5820a12f","sha1":"3a314211fd44c07c2e022b842c2799ee55e3945f","format":"Metadata"}],"files_count":31,"item_last_updated":1663923487,"item_size":6041631645,"metadata":{"identifier":"snake-milking","mediatype":"movies","collection":["opensource_movies","community"],"creator":"Joaquim Baeta","date":"2022-09-22","description":"<div>Producing antivenom starts with snake milking. A skilled (and brave!) \nherpetologist needs to coax a venomous snake into relinquishing its \nvenom, which is precious and limited in supply. This encompasses a \nvariety of techniques, first among them the ability to calmly handle a \nsnake that could turn on you at any moment.\n\n<br /></div><div><br /></div><div>CHAPTERS:</div><div><br /></div><div>0:06 Intro <br /></div><div>0:28 What is snake milking? </div><div>0:49 Juvenile Calloselasma rhodostoma (Malayan pit viper) <br /></div><div>2:04 Adult Calloselasma rhodostoma (Malayan pit viper) <br /></div><div>2:54 Bungarus fasciatus (banded krait) <br /></div><div>3:35 Storing the snake venom <br /></div><div>4:32 The importance of this work <br /></div><div>4:59 Credits <br /></div><div><br /></div><div>CREDITS: <br /></div><div><br /></div><div>Shot, edited, and directed by Joaquim Baeta <br /></div><div><br /></div><div>Narrated by Donan Satria Yudha (Lecturer in the Laboratory of Animal \nSystematics, Faculty of Biology, Universitas Gadjah Mada) <br /></div><div><br /></div><div>Produced by Lelly Marliana</div><div><br /></div><div>\u00a0Snake milking performed by Dr. drh. Slamet Raharjo, M.P. (Lecturer in \nthe Department of Internal Medicine, Faculty of Veterinary Medicine, \nUniversitas Gadjah Mada)</div><div><br /></div><div>Snake milking assistants were Rahma Izzati, Ananto Puradi Nainggolan, \nNoorman Hendry Fauzy, Saliyo, Dino Ashar Setiawan, and Anindwi Nugra \nAfianto, S.K.H.</div><div><br /></div><div>\"Blackout &amp; Blue\" by Little Glass Men, https://freemusicarchive.org/music/Little_Glass_Men/Debut_EP, CC BY 4.0 <br /></div><div><br /></div><div>Snake icon by Andrew Doane, https://thenounproject.com/icon/snake-1173205, CC BY 3.0 <br /></div><div><br /></div><div>Bungarus candidus photo by Wibowo Djatmiko, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bungar_candi_120608-0338_krw.jpg, CC BY-SA 3.0 <br /></div><div><br /></div><div>Filmed at the Laboratory of Animal Systematics, Universitas Gadjah Mada <br /></div><div><br /></div><div>___</div><div><br /></div><div>Support the Scenoptica project on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/scenoptica<br /></div><div>Ko-fi: https://ko-fi.com/scenoptica<br /></div><div>Website: https://scenoptica.com<br /></div><div>Twitter: https://twitter.com/scenoptica<br /></div>","language":"eng","licenseurl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","scanner":"Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.7.0","subject":["snake milking","venomous","snake","venom extraction","viper","krait","fang","calloselasma","rhodostoma","bungarus","fasciatus","antivenom","ugm","universitas gadjah mada"],"title":"Snake Milki